  "uncertainty_note": "Bands and errors are the plotted values. See the figure caption for confidence level and estimator.",
  "data_note": "Exact numerical artist inputs in plotted units; no values have been digitised from a PDF or recomputed from curves.",
  "caption_latex": "Independent five-site controller controls from the explicit-cavity SSE. {(a):} Signed endpoint correlation $G_{15}^{zz}$ for one controller, three controllers sharing the same summed squared gain (equal budget), and three controllers each at the full single-site gain. {(b)} $G_{15}^{yy}$ for the equal-budget controller, the same gains with detection efficiencies reduced to $1/3$ (equal detection), and the equal-budget controller with the gains on sites 2 and 4 reversed in sign. {(c)} $G_{15}^{zz}$ with feedback off, full-gain feedback, and independent noise at the same full gains. {(d):} Mean total photon population $\\sum_j\\langle n_j\\rangle$ for the three cases in {(c)}. {The plots in} {(a,c)} share a vertical scale. {The no-feedback, one-controller, equal-budget, full-gain and noise-only conditions contain 768, 1536, 768, 1536 and 1024 paths, respectively. Equal-detection and reversed-sign controls each contain 64 paths. All correlation bands are pointwise 95\\% whole-block intervals, with antithetic partners resampled together and connected moments formed after averaging the density. The photon curves in (d) use the corresponding path-weighted means without bands because photon moments were retained only as batch averages. Full gain is orange, equal budget purple and one controller teal; no feedback is grey and independent noise charcoal. In (b), equal detection is teal and reversed sign orange.} Greater photon population under independent drive noise does not reproduce the correlation response. These are mechanism controls, not reduced-root HOPS trajectories."
